Fair enough (especially considering an early-game QM could very easily
drink a gain level potion and turn from a standard annoyance into a
nightmare.)

How about two types?

Master QM (appears in mid-game, around umber-hulk/Olog-hai/dragon
time): item teleports stay on-level.

Arch QM: (appears in late game, i.e. after castle): item teleports
stay on-level 50% of the time, the other 50% they go off-level in a
quantum-mechanical fashion (i.e. ~90% of the time they will tend to
stay in fairly close range, +/- 1-3 levels, but *could* end up
absolutely anywhere in the dungeon.)

Arch QMs would have more hit points, be harder to kill, and their
corpses would have a higher chance of granting teleport control.

